WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.512
You've run agent swarms before. They all say done.

2
00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:10.982
The Perfect Orchestrator is different. One lead session commands a fleet of real Claude Code workers in tmux.

3
00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:16.667
It writes each worker a brief. Watches them work. Nudges the ones that drift.

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.930
Workers coordinate on a file bus. No servers. No daemons. No magic.

5
00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:29.019
And before anything reaches you — a different worker tries to tear each result apart.

6
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.790
What survives is what ships.

7
00:00:32.921 --> 00:00:38.270
The Perfect Orchestrator. One prompt. A fleet of workers. Every result verified.
